Like...

```javascript
options = options || {};
if ('enabled' in options) {
    if ('level' in options) {
        if (Boolean(options.level) !== Boolean(options.enabled)) {
            throw new Error('Invalid options; cannot have differing .level and .enabled values for Chalk constructor');
        }
    }

    this.enabled = options.enabled;
    this.level = options.enabled ? 1 : ('level' in options ? options.level : 0);
} else {
    var level = 'level' in options ? options.level : supportsColor.level;
    this.enabled = Boolean(level);
    this.level = level;
}
```

Something like that, just to maintain backwards compatibility, based on the comments here.

